# =============================================================================
# Build artefacts. None of this belongs in the repo -- it is all regenerable
# from the sources by `make`.
#
# This file exists because these directories were committed once already and
# had to be removed by hand (see "removed unnecessary object files"). Without
# it, `git clean -fd` is also unusable: the optim core's sources sit untracked
# until first commit, so a blind clean deletes real work along with the junk.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C++ build output (Makefile BUILD_DIR)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verilator. One obj_dir per configuration: obj_dir_optim_hu, obj_dir_opt_pl,
# obj_dir_poly4_dsp_axi, ... roughly 700 KB each and there are dozens.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
obj_dir/
obj_dir_*/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vivado. .Xil is scratch state; the journals and logs land wherever vivado
# happened to be launched from, which includes scripts/.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Xil/
*.jou
*.log
*.str
*.pb
*.rpx
*.dcp
.cache/
.hbs/
vivado_pid*.zip
hs_err_pid*.log

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiler / editor leftovers
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.o
*.d
*.a
*.so
*.gch
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
compile_commands.json
